<h1>Slack approval intake</h1>

<p>
  Slack is the <strong>remote control</strong>; Postgres is the <strong>record</strong>.
  A proposal's card carries Approve, Reject and Correct buttons, and a click travels
  the same path as the form on
  <%= link_to "the proposals queue", admin_proposals_path %>: signed payload &rarr;
  write the decision to the proposal row &rarr; execute &rarr; update the card. The
  card is updated <em>last</em> and is allowed to fail, because a stale card with a
  correct row is recoverable and the reverse is not. If Slack is down, every
  decision is still available here — an outage costs convenience, not authority.
</p>

<% unless @settings.configured? %>
  <p class="concierge-flash concierge-flash--alert">
    No Slack signing secret is configured, so <code>/concierge/slack/events</code> and
    <code>/concierge/slack/interactions</code> answer 404. Nothing can be signed, so
    nothing is trusted.
  </p>
<% end %>

<h2>Endpoints</h2>

<dl>
  <dt>Events</dt>
  <dd><code>POST <%= slack_events_path %></code> — Slack's URL handshake, and replies humans type in a case thread (each becomes a captured correction).</dd>

  <dt>Interactivity</dt>
  <dd><code>POST <%= slack_interactions_path %></code> — the buttons and the two modals. This is why the seam needs a real Slack app rather than an incoming webhook: a webhook cannot tell you who clicked.</dd>

  <dt>Signature</dt>
  <dd>
    <%= @settings.configured? ? "verified on every request (v0 HMAC-SHA256, 5-minute replay window)" : "not configured" %>
  </dd>

  <dt>Posting</dt>
  <dd><%= @settings.can_post? ? "a bot token or transport is configured" : "no bot token — cards cannot be posted, decisions can still be received" %></dd>

  <dt>Who clicked</dt>
  <dd>
    <%= @settings.actor_for ? "mapped to a host identity by config.slack { actor_for … }" : "recorded as the Slack user id (slack:U…) — map it with config.slack { actor_for … }" %>
  </dd>
</dl>

<h2>One channel per agent</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Agent</th><th>Channel</th><th>Cards today</th><th>Daily cap</th>
      <th>Suppressed</th><th>Failed</th><th>Awaiting a human</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @agents.each do |agent| %>
      <% slug = agent.slug.to_s %>
      <tr>
        <th><%= slug %><%= " — off" unless agent.enabled? %></th>
        <td>
          <% if @settings.channel(slug) %>
            <code><%= @settings.channel(slug) %></code>
          <% else %>
            <em>none — this agent posts no cards</em>
          <% end %>
        </td>
        <td><%= @posted_today[slug] || 0 %></td>
        <td><%= @settings.daily_card_cap || "unlimited" %></td>
        <td><%= @suppressed[slug] || 0 %></td>
        <td><%= @failed[slug] || 0 %></td>
        <td><%= @awaiting[slug] || 0 %></td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>
  The cap is per agent per day: one business function cannot make a channel
  unreadable. Over it, the card is not posted and the suppression is recorded — the
  proposal is untouched and still waiting in the queue. Autonomous work never gets a
  card at all; it arrives as a periodic digest (<code>Concierge::SlackDigestJob</code>),
  because a notification nobody can act on is how the refund card gets scrolled past.
</p>

<h2>Recent cards</h2>

<% if @cards.none? %>
  <p><em>No cards yet.</em></p>
<% else %>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Card</th><th>Agent</th><th>Case</th><th>Proposal</th>
        <th>State</th><th>Thread</th><th>Posted</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @cards.each do |card| %>
        <tr>
          <td>#<%= card.id %></td>
          <td><%= card.agent_slug %></td>
          <td><%= card.subject_type %>#<%= card.subject_id %></td>
          <td>
            <%= link_to "##{card.agent_proposal_id}", admin_proposals_path %>
          </td>
          <td>
            <%= card.state %>
            <% if card.failed? %>
              <br><strong><%= card.error %></strong>
            <% elsif card.suppressed? %>
              <br>over the daily cap — decide it in the queue
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td>
            <% if card.thread_ts.present? %>
              <code><%= card.thread_ts %></code>
              <%= "(root)" if card.thread_ts == card.message_ts %>
            <% else %>
              —
            <% end %>
          </td>
          <td><%= card.posted_at || "—" %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
<% end %>
